      {
        "area": "Index read-modify-write cycle",
        "description": "Every new entry requires reading the entire index, modifying, and writing the entire index back. For knowledge-base/index.json, this costs 24373 chars read + 24973 chars write = 49346 chars for adding ~600 chars of content.",
        "waste_tokens": 12186,
        "improvement": "Append-only indexes or database-backed storage would eliminate the full read-write cycle"
      },
      {
        "area": "Large SOP documents for simple lookups",
        "description": "tool_sops.json (52576 chars) and sop_013_prompt_engineering.json (43484 chars) must be read in full even when an agent only needs one section.",
        "waste_tokens": 24015,
        "improvement": "Split large SOPs into smaller section files, or provide a table-of-contents with section offsets"
      },
      {
        "area": "Template overhead per write",
        "description": "Agents must read and mentally parse template files (total 2022 chars) before every write operation, even when familiar with the format.",
        "waste_tokens": 506,
        "improvement": "Templates could be internalized or provided as structured schemas rather than markdown to fill"
      }
    ],
    "recommended_priorities": [
      "1. Replace full-index reads with queryable API (saves ~6900 tokens per index lookup, estimated 10+ lookups per session = 69000+ tokens saved)",
      "2. Split tool_sops.json (13144 tokens) and sop_013 (10871 tokens) into smaller section files",
      "3. Implement append-only index updates (saves reading+rewriting ~12000 tokens per index update)",
      "4. Create summary/pointer files for large KB entries (KB-0015, KB-0016, KB-0017 are 25000+ chars each)",
      "5. Compress redundant by_data_type and tag_index sections in index files (storage/sources/index.json: 17000+ chars of by_data_type index alone)"
